# "After finished: Save/Delete" toggle (DSTYLE_LONG_EXISTING row 2) on a
# STOPPED (idle) timer.
#
# CORRECTED after a live run: this does NOT just flip a flag for a stopped
# timer - del_confirm_do() (main.c) deletes it immediately on confirmation
# (DELCONF_TOGGLE_STOPPED), since there's no future "finish" event left to
# defer the decision to. That's only a real, later-deferred toggle for a
# RUNNING timer (DELCONF_TOGGLE_RUNNING, which just sets s_delete_on_
# finish[idx]=true and keeps running) - see
# after_finished_toggle_delete_to_save.seq for that case instead.
#
# Live-verified: TAP down (off "+ New timer", row 0, onto the just-seeded
# timer) + LONGPRESS select actually opens the edit menu; row 2 = "After
# finished"; the confirm menu's row 0 = "Delete".
IMPORT ../common/wipe_and_prep.seq

APPMSG --string 10000="$(printf 'Quick Timer\0375\0371')"
SLEEP 1
SCREENSHOT initial_idle

# "+ New timer" sits at row 0 (moved to the top of the list) and is where
# a fresh list's selection defaults to - ml_select_long() is a deliberate
# no-op on that row (see main.c's ml_resolve_selected_target/is_new
# check), so long-pressing without first moving off it does nothing at
# all. One DOWN moves selection onto the just-seeded timer row.
TAP down
LONGPRESS select
SCREENSHOT edit_menu
TAP down
TAP down
SCREENSHOT after_finished_row_selected
TAP select
SLEEP 1
SCREENSHOT delete_confirm_shown

# Confirming "Delete" here deletes the timer immediately - no snoozing,
# no waiting for it to fire.
TAP select
SLEEP 1
SCREENSHOT should_be_gone_from_list_immediately
